Note on Exo (GPL-3.0):

Exo (https://github.com/exo-explore/exo) is licensed under GPL-3.0.
loke does NOT link to or include Exo. Exo is an optional, separate
process that communicates with loke exclusively via its REST API.
This architectural boundary ensures loke's Apache 2.0 licence is
not affected by Exo's GPL-3.0 licence. See docs/epics-and-stories.md
(story F8.4) for details on this boundary.

================================================================================
Bundled datasets
================================================================================

The demo application bundles snapshots of third-party open data so that it works
offline. Each snapshot is a derived work, not the original: every transformation
applied is recorded in packages/moke/static/data/manifest.json, and a licence
sidecar sits beside each CSV so the file remains self-describing if copied out of
this repository.

Attribution as required by the respective licences:

  Australian Road Deaths Database (ARDD) — Fatalities
    Source: Bureau of Infrastructure and Transport Research Economics (BITRE),
    Australian Road Deaths Database. Licensed under Creative Commons Attribution
    3.0 Australia.
    http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/au/

Datasets whose terms have not been confirmed as permitting redistribution are
deliberately NOT bundled and are fetched live instead. scripts/fetch_opendata.py
aborts rather than committing a snapshot whose declared licence differs from what
its recipe expects.

Synthetic demonstration data shipped with the demo is authored for this project
and is not government data, regardless of the domain it imitates. It is marked
kind: synthetic in the manifest so the two cannot be confused.
